ads it back; finish by reading the whole lesson together","Slate work: copy “She is kind.”","Talk about one kind thing your child can do for someone today"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XIV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00151"}],"questions":["Why can''t the old man see?","How does Mary help him?"],"answers":["He is blind","She holds him by the hand"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-3-5","title":"Lesson XV: Review","steps":["Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “Nell is kind to him.”","Retell the review in your own words: who is kind, and who gets the eggs?"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00158"}],"questions":["Who will get the eggs?","Who will feed the ducks?"],"answers":["Mary","Tom"],"notes":"Review lesson: no new words. Let your child read it as independently as possible and note any words to revisit."}]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-u4","title":"Unit 4: Lessons XVI–XX","lessons":[{"id":"mcguffey-primer-4-1","title":"Lesson XVI: Sue''s Doll","steps":["New words: Sue, doll, dress, new, her, let; sound focus: ew","Read it once aloud for your child, then have them read it to you (or to a sibling or stuffed animal)","Slate work: copy “Sue has a doll.”","Play out the lesson with a doll or stuffed toy"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XVI","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00164"}],"questions":["What is new on the doll?","Who gets to hold the doll?"],"answers":["Its dress","Ann"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-4-2","title":"Lesson XVII: The Bird''s Nest","steps":["New words: there, five, bird, tree, rob, do; sound focus: long i (five); v","Read the lesson aloud together, pointing to each word; then let your child read it alone","Slate work: copy “Do not rob the nest.”","Count to five on fingers for the eggs, then tell why we leave nests alone"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XVII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00172"}],"questions":["How many eggs are in the nest?","What should we not do?"],"answers":["Five","Rob the nest"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-4-3","title":"Lesson XVIII: The Pet Bird","steps":["New words: cage, pet, sing, lives, so, loves; sound focus: ng; soft g (cage)","You read a line, then your child reads it back; finish by reading the whole lesson together","Slate work: copy “It lives in a new cage.”","Narrate: tell three things about Sue''s bird"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XVIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00179"}],"questions":["Where does the pet bird live?","What does the bird do on Sue''s hand?"],"answers":["In a new cage","It sings"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-4-4","title":"Lesson XIX: Boys at Play","steps":["New words: are, you, yes, fast, too, like, boys, of, play; sound focus: oy; long a (play)","Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “I like to see boys play.”","Look at the snowy picture and name the games you see"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XIX","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00188"}],"questions":["How many boys are playing?","Why can''t Tom run fast?","Who can catch Tom?"],"answers":["Five","He is too fat","Nat"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-4-5","title":"Lesson XX: Review","steps":["Read it once aloud for your child, then have them read it to you (or to a sibling or stuffed animal)","Slate work: copy “Sue has a new dress.”","Read the script exercise and copy one line"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XX","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00198"}],"questions":["What two things does Sue have?","Why won''t Tom rob a nest?"],"answers":["A doll and a pet bird","He is too kind"],"notes":"Review lesson: no new words. Let your child read it as independently as possible and note any word