 lesson aloud together, pointing to each word; then let your child read it alone","Slate work: copy “She likes to ride in her cart.”","Narrate: why do the goats love Bess?"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIII","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00310"}],"questions":["What pulls Bess''s cart?","Why do the goats love Bess?"],"answers":["Two goats","She feeds them and is kind to them"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-4","title":"Lesson XXXIV: The House on Fire","steps":["New words: blaze, put, yet, house, fire, roof, call, ring, we; sound focus: z","You read a line, then your child reads it back; finish by reading the whole lesson together","Slate work: copy “Run, boys, and ring the bell.”","Talk about what your family would do in a fire"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXIV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00319"}],"questions":["What part of the house is in a blaze?","What are the boys told to do?"],"answers":["The roof","Ring the bell and call men to put out the fire"]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-7-5","title":"Lesson XXXV: Review: Tom and Bess","steps":["Let your child read the lesson aloud slowly; help only on words they can''t sound out","Slate work: copy “We can ride to the mill.”","Read it as a play: you are Tom, your child is Bess"],"links":[{"label":"Read Lesson XXXV","url":"https://www.gutenberg.org/cache/epub/14642/pg14642-images.html#id00327"}],"questions":["How are the logs cut at the mill?","How will Tom and Bess get to the mill?"],"answers":["With a saw","Ride in the goat cart"],"notes":"Review lesson: no new words. Let your child read it as independently as possible and note any words to revisit. Written as a conversation; it reads well with two voices."}]},{"id":"mcguffey-primer-u8","title":"Unit 8: Lessons XXXVI–XL","lessons":[{"id":"mcguffey-primer-8-1","title":"Lesson XXXVI: Miss May''s Rule","steps":["New words: Miss, wants, would, tells, rule, keep, good, that, each; sound focus