ddition (continued)","steps":["Add three small piles of beans together","Finish the second review set aloud","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXII (p. 24)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n30/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 24","questions":["How many are 6 and 6 and 3?","How many are 4 and 9?","How many are 7 and 2 and 8?"],"answers":["15","13","17"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-4-8","title":"Lesson XXIII: Addition Problems","steps":["Act out a shopping story with pennies","Read each word problem and answer with a full sentence","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXIII (p. 26)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n32/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 26","questions":["Ann paid 4 cents for a pencil, 3 for paper, and 5 for a ribbon. How much in all?","Three boys caught 2, 6, and 5 fish. How many fish?","A girl has 7 dolls and gets 8 more. How many dolls?"],"answers":["12 cents","13","15"]}]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-u5","title":"Unit 5: Subtraction, Taking 1 to 5 (Lessons XXIV–XXIX)","lessons":[{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-1","title":"Lesson XXIV: Subtraction: Owls and Bats","steps":["Set out 7 toys; take some away and count what is left","Look at the owls-and-bats picture and answer the questions","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXIV (p. 27)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n33/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 27","questions":["Five owls sat on a branch; 3 flew away. How many were left?","Eight bats were flying; 6 went into a barn. How many still flying?","Six less 4 are how many?"],"answers":["2","2","2"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-2","title":"Lesson XXV: Subtraction: Taking 1","steps":["Take one bean at a time from a pile","Recite ''1 from 1 leaves 0…'' and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXV (p. 28)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n34/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 28","questions":["1 from 9 leaves how many?","Jim had 7 apples and ate 1. How many left?","1 from 11 leaves how many?"],"answers":["8","6","10"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-3","title":"Lesson XXVI: Subtraction: Taking 2","steps":["Take pairs of buttons away from a pile","Recite the 2s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXVI (p. 29)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n35/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 29","questions":["2 from 9 leaves how many?","Kate had 8 cents and spent 2. How many left?","2 from 12 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","6 cents","10"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-4","title":"Lesson XXVII: Subtraction: Taking 3","steps":["Remove 3 blocks from towers of different sizes","Recite the 3s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXVII (p. 30)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n36/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 30","questions":["3 from 10 leaves how many?","A nest had 6 eggs; 3 hatched. How many have not hatched?","3 from 12 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","3","9"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-5","title":"Lesson XXVIII: Subtraction: Taking 4","steps":["Take 4 spoons from a drawer pile","Recite the 4s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXVIII (p. 31)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n37/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 31","questions":["4 from 11 leaves how many?","There were 9 pears; 4 were eaten. How many left?","4 from 13 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","5","9"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-5-6","title":"Lesson XXIX: Subtraction: Taking 5","steps":["Hide one hand of 5 fingers to show taking 5","Recite the 5s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXIX (p. 32)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n38/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 32","questions":["5 from 12 leaves how many?","Ned had 14 marbles and lost 5. How many now?","5 from 9 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","9","4"]}]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-u6","title":"Unit 6: Subtraction, Taking 6 to 10 and Review (Lessons XXX–XXXVII)","lessons":[{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-1","title":"Lesson XXX: Subtraction: Taking 6","steps":["Take 6 eggs from a carton of 12 and count what remains","Recite the 6s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXX (p. 33)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n39/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 33","questions":["6 from 13 leaves how many?","A baker had 15 rolls and sold 6. How many left?","6 from 10 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","9","4"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-2","title":"Lesson XXXI: Subtraction: Taking 7","steps":["Use 7 days of the week; cross off days","Recite the 7s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXXI (p. 34)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n40/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 34","questions":["7 from 15 leaves how many?","Sue had 12 ribbons and gave away 7. How many left?","7 from 11 leaves how many?"],"answers":["8","5","4"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-3","title":"Lesson XXXII: Subtraction: Taking 8","steps":["Remove 8 crayons from a box of 16","Recite the 8s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXXII (p. 35)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n41/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 35","questions":["8 from 14 leaves how many?","There were 17 sheep; 8 went into the barn. How many outside?","8 from 12 leaves how many?"],"answers":["6","9","4"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-4","title":"Lesson XXXIII: Subtraction: Taking 9","steps":["Take 9 from a pile by taking 10 and putting 1 back","Recite the 9s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXXIII (p. 36)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n42/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 36","questions":["9 from 16 leaves how many?","Tom had 13 cents and spent 9. How many left?","9 from 18 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","4 cents","9"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-5","title":"Lesson XXXIV: Subtraction: Taking 10","steps":["Remove a ten-bundle from bundles and loose straws","Recite the 10s subtraction table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXXIV (p. 37)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n43/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 37","questions":["10 from 17 leaves how many?","A tree had 19 apples; 10 fell. How many still on the tree?","10 from 20 leaves how many?"],"answers":["7","9","10"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-6","title":"Lesson XXXV: Review of Subtraction","steps":["Play ''how many left?'' by hiding beans under a cup","Work the review questions using the word ''less''","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XXXV (p. 38)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n44/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 38","questions":["How many are 11 less 5?","How many are 14 less 8?","How many are 9 less 6?"],"answers":["6","6","3"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-6-7","title":"Lesson XXXVI: Addition and Subtraction Together","steps":["Add two piles of beans, then take some 