ps://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n48/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 42","questions":["How many are 7 times 1?","Figs cost 1 cent each. What do 9 figs cost?","How many are 1 time 5?"],"answers":["7","9 cents","5"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-7-3","title":"Lesson XL: Multiplication: Times 2","steps":["Pair socks and count by 2s","Recite the 2s times table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XL (p. 43)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n49/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 43","questions":["How many are 2 times 6?","Each child has 2 shoes. How many shoes do 7 children have?","How many are 9 times 2?"],"answers":["12","14","18"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-7-4","title":"Lesson XLI: Multiplication: Times 3","steps":["Make 3-leaf clovers from paper and count leaves","Recite the 3s times table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XLI (p. 44)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n50/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 44","questions":["How many are 3 times 5?","Pencils are 3 cents each. What do 6 cost?","How many are 3 times 8?"],"answers":["15","18 cents","24"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-7-5","title":"Lesson XLII: Multiplication: Times 4","steps":["Count the legs on 4-legged toys or chairs","Recite the 4s times table and work the problems","Solve the 3 practice problems below, using objects if needed"],"links":[{"label":"Lesson XLII (p. 45)","url":"https://archive.org/details/raysnewprimarya00raygoog/page/n51/mode/1up"}],"pages":"p. 45","questions":["How many are 4 times 6?","Each wagon has 4 wheels. How many wheels on 5 wagons?","How many are 4 times 9?"],"answers":["24","20","36"]},{"id":"rays-primary-arithmetic-7-6","title":"Lesson XLIII: Multiplication: Times 5","steps":["Count nickels by 5s","Recite the 5s times table and work the problems","Solve the 